\begin{definition}
A matrix $A$ is called strictly column diagonally balanced dominant if there exists a diagonal matrix $D$ such that $|AD| + |D A^T|$ is strictly column diagonally dominant. Furthermore, if all the diagonal elements of $AD + D A^T $ are positive then the matrix $A$ is called positive diagonally balanced dominant. 
\end{definition}

